BOMs (EF BB BF) stripped byte-exactly (each file lost exactly 3 bytes, nothing else) from SYSTEM_MANIFEST.json, constitution/constitutional_rules.json, constitution/promotion_policy.json, constitution/risk_policy.json, library/config/clu_runtime_policy.json, synthesis/synthesis_contract.json. Strict utf-8 JSON parsers rejected all six before the fix (JSONDecodeError 'Unexpected UTF-8 BOM'); both strict and sig parsers accept them after. New hashes recorded in the bundle.

sovereign_product/server.py _write_manifest wrote SYSTEM_MANIFEST.json back with encoding='utf-8-sig', re-adding the BOM on every manifest update — changed to plain utf-8 so the strip sticks. Readers verified byte-level: system_manifest.py:185 and server.py:398 read utf-8-sig (accepts BOM-less content); server.py compiles.

New regression guard tools/release/check_governance_bom.py (explicit enumeration of the six paths, no globs) + 5 tests incl. real-worktree strict-parse proof.

